# GUI app feature parity (egui ↔ SpecChumMac ↔ Windows shell)

Spec Chum has multiple first-party GUI hosts that must stay **feature-aligned**:

| Host | Path |
| --- | --- |
| egui | `crates/app` (`spec_chum`) — cross-platform / Linux / Windows release primary |
| SpecChumMac | `apps/macos` + `living_room` / `host_api` FFI — macOS product shell |
| Windows Win32 shell | `crates/windows_shell` (`spec_chum_windows`) — optional native Windows host ([#351](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/issues/351)); egui remains release primary until packaging switches |

## Feature parity (mandatory)

- **Same product features** on every shipped / in-tree host unless a capability is **genuinely platform-specific** (e.g. IOSurface / Metal living-room on macOS, Win32-only window chrome, Linux absence of a second shell).
- Shared behaviour lives in shared Rust (`control_plane`, `host_api`, `machine`, …). Hosts are thin adapters.
- Agent Debug HTTP, tape/disk/media, input, Debug/inspect, prefs that map to `UiPreferences` / session prefs, and host screenshots (`/v1/framebuffer`, `/v1/host/display`, `/v1/host/window`) are **not** egui-only or Mac-only.
- When adding or changing a GUI-visible or agent-visible feature: **update every first-party host that exposes GUI** (or the shared backend all use) in the **same PR**, plus docs (`docs/MACOS_NATIVE.md`, `docs/WINDOWS_NATIVE.md`, `docs/AGENT_DEBUG_API.md`, `AGENTS.md` as needed).
- **Never defer host parity.** Do not ship “works in egui, SpecChumMac/Windows later” (or the reverse), even with a follow-up issue — except when a host is still a documented **vertical slice** whose open checklist explicitly defers deeper panels (see [#351](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/issues/351) / `docs/WINDOWS_NATIVE.md`). Media open, tape transport, agent HTTP, and inspect/status must not silently diverge.

## Visual / UX chrome (platform HIG — allowed divergence)

Make the GUIs **as similar as possible in product capabilities** while **respecting platform HIG** for chrome:

| May differ by platform | Must not differ |
| --- | --- |
| Window chrome, menu bar layout, spacing, materials (SwiftUI / Fluent / egui) | Which product features exist (media types, hardware attach, agent routes, prefs semantics) |
| Shortcut modifiers (⌘ on macOS, Ctrl on Windows) for the **same** action | Action meaning / guest behaviour |
| File dialog look (`NSOpenPanel` vs Win32/`rfd` vs egui) | Filters / supported formats / load path semantics |
| Presentation blit path (egui texture vs `SpectrumDisplayView` vs GDI) | Framebuffer contents / timing ownership in Rust |

Do **not** invent divergent product features “because HIG.” Do **not** force macOS-looking UI onto Windows (or vice versa).

## Platform-specific (allowed)

- Presentation path only: egui texture vs SpecChumMac `SpectrumDisplayView` / living-room IOSurface vs Windows `StretchDIBits`.
- OS window chrome / menu bar / sandbox / signing / installers.
- Capture plumbing may differ (eframe `NSView` vs `sc_agent_set_host_window_id` vs Win32 HWND) but the **HTTP surface and semantics** must match.
- Living-room 3D CRT remains Metal/wgpu-gated; absence on a host that cannot present it is OK if documented.

## Check before finishing

- Grep `crates/app`, `apps/macos`, and `crates/windows_shell` (plus `living_room` agent FFI) for the feature.
- If `SPEC_CHUM_AGENT=1` embed is involved, verify SpecChumMac `HostBridge` + `sc_agent_*`, egui embed, and Windows `SPEC_CHUM_AGENT` path.
- Rebuild SpecChumMac when living_room / host_api / agent routes change (`./scripts/build_macos_app.sh` / `run_macos_app.sh`); build Windows shell on Windows CI / `scripts/build_windows_app.ps1` when that host is touched.
- If any first-party host is missing a product feature that another exposes (outside an explicit vertical-slice deferral), the work is not finished — do not file a follow-up and move on.
